  "battleListAppBarTitle": "Battle — Logic Check",
  "battleInfoTooltip": "What is Logic Check?",
  "battleInfoSheetTitle": "What is a Logic Check (challenge battle)?",
  "battleInfoSheetIntro": "A way to openly verify whether a post's claim actually holds up, through a TP-staked counter-post and audience judging.",
  "battleInfoSheetStep1Title": "1. Challenge",
  "battleInfoSheetStep1Body": "If you disagree with a post's claim, you can stake TP to create a counter-post, which is structured as a paired battle against the original post.",
  "battleInfoSheetStep2Title": "2. Audience betting",
  "battleInfoSheetStep2Body": "Other users can bet TP on which side is more logically sound. Correct bets earn a payout, but TP is an internal point that cannot be cashed out.",
  "battleInfoSheetStep3Title": "3. Judging",
  "battleInfoSheetStep3Body": "Over a set window (roughly 24–72 hours), audience votes and top-tier judges decide the winner.",
  "battleInfoSheetStep4Title": "4. Broken-logic penalty",
  "battleInfoSheetStep4Body": "If enough top-5% judges flag a post as \"broken logic,\" it gets a warning badge and stops spreading (the post itself is not deleted). To prevent false positives, this requires a minimum quorum of judges and includes an appeal process.",
